# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Nothing here is a real secret — the local values match
# docker-compose.yml, and the hosted ones are placeholders.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#   docker compose up -d      # local Postgres (needs Docker Desktop)
#   npm run db:push           # apply lib/db/schema.ts
#
# The three hosted services below are the ones docs/02 (ADR-7) settled on: Neon, Cloudflare R2 and
# Clerk. Only the first is wired.

# ── Database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development: matches the user/password/db in docker-compose.yml.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://eve:eve@localhost:5432/eve

# Neon (production). Dashboard → Connection Details.
# Use the POOLED string — the host with `-pooler` in it — from the app: a serverless function opens
# a connection per invocation and will exhaust a direct pool. Migrations want the DIRECT host,
# because they need a real session.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@ep-<id>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/eve?sslmode=require
# DIRECT_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@ep-<id>.<region>.aws.neon.tech/eve?sslmode=require
#
# ⚠ DIRECT_URL is documentation right now, not wiring: drizzle.config.ts reads DATABASE_URL like
# everything else does. Teaching it to prefer DIRECT_URL is a one-line change, and the day Neon
# goes in is the day to make it — running a migration through the pooler is how you get a hung
# `db:push` with no error to read.

# ── Cloudflare R2 — file storage (not wired yet) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gallery photos, product images, venue plan underlays. S3-compatible: the browser PUTs straight
# into the bucket with a presigned URL, so these credentials stay server-only and none of them may
# become a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=eve-media
#
# Reads are served by a custom domain on the bucket, never through the Node process — which is the
# whole reason photographs are cheap here: egress out of R2 is free.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://media.eve.studio

# ── Clerk — auth (not wired yet; replaces lib/auth/, see ADR-10) ───────────────────────────────
# The publishable key is public and ships to the browser. The secret key is server-only, must never
# appear in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, and must never be committed.
# Roles and tenancy stay in our own tables — Clerk answers "who", and nothing else.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
